From: plumOS RG280V port
Subject: [PATCH] clocksource: ingenic-ost: keep OST running through suspend

The JZ4770 RG280V hangs in the OST noirq suspend callback when the
clocksource is gated. Keeping the OST clock enabled lets all PM test stages
return and lets the physical power key resume from deep suspend. Tested on
RG280V with the plumOS power menu.

---
 drivers/clocksource/ingenic-ost.c | 13 ++-----------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clocksource/ingenic-ost.c b/drivers/clocksource/ingenic-ost.c
--- a/drivers/clocksource/ingenic-ost.c
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/ingenic-ost.c
@@ -143,18 +143,13 @@ static int __init ingenic_ost_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 static int ingenic_ost_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
-	struct ingenic_ost *ost = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
-
-	clk_disable(ost->clk);
-
+	/* Keep the active clocksource running during system suspend. */
 	return 0;
 }
 
 static int ingenic_ost_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
-	struct ingenic_ost *ost = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
-
-	return clk_enable(ost->clk);
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops ingenic_ost_pm_ops = {
